      ],
      "text": "This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 6.5 score.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.16754150390625,
        132.47508239746094,
        509.7934875488281,
        194.3102264404297
      ],
      "text": "Mobile phones, nowadays, contains essential features with entertainment also. There has been a\nlarge growth seen in usage hours of smartphones among youngsters. There are several reasons\nbehind this situation and | find this development more beneficial than negative. Both the reasons\nand my view is elaborated further.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        60.18621826171875,
        203.12844848632812,
        520.51904296875,
        233.23562622070312
      ],
      "text": "The first reason for overusage of smart devices by youngsters is the social benefit they provide.\nThe smart phone connected with internet opens up the large possibilities, from creating new friends\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        60.84041213989258,
        235.18417358398438,
        515.6943969726562,
        330.0565490722656
      ],
      "text": "fo communicating with them over social media. For instance, a child in my neighbourhood chats\nfor hours with his school friends over Facebook (a social media) and also spend time over online\nvideo sharing phone application. Moreover, the mobile gaming, specially multiplayer games, is\nanother major reason for the situation. Children plays different kind of games over mobile for the\nentertainment purpose and they involve themselves in games in such a manner, that they forget\nabout the timing and other work to do.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        60.84047317504883,
        338.2203063964844,
        511.4028015136719,
        400.71026611328125
      ],
      "text": "However, | believe that smartphones have also increased the knowledge of pupils. It has developed\nsome important social skills, such as communication skill, team work and many more, by allowing\nthem to work and play in groups, without the restriction of distance. In addition, children can\nlearn through internet by watchin online videos and reading articles, which ultimately helps them\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.1676025390625,
        402.98590087890625,
        522.39013671875,
        433.420166015625
      ],
      "text": "in their studies as well as language skills. For example, whenever my niece require to Know about\nsomething, he searches it over the internet and learns from it. Moreover, multiplayer online gaming\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.82182693481445,
        435.0415954589844,
        448.3365478515625,
        449.12091064453125
      ],
      "text": "improves their multitasking ability and it also gives them a competitive environment\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.49475860595703,
        457.6114196777344,
        509.2522888183594,
        487.3914794921875
      ],
      "text": "Overall,\n| agree that overusage of smartphones on regular basis is harmful for them, but if given\nproper guidance, mobile phones can help them in learning some life-long skills.\n"
    },
